 <title>Paul McCartney becomes a billionaire and world’s third richest musician</title>
 <link>https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/nov/09/paul-mccartney-billionaire</link>
 <description>&lt;p&gt;According to a new analysis by Forbes, the former Beatle now has a net worth of $1.4bn, placing him behind Jay-Z and Taylor Swift&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Paul McCartney has joined the ranks of the world’s billionaires. &lt;a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/the-billie/2026/11/09/the-14-billion-beatle-how-paul-mccartney-became-the-worlds-third-richest-musician/"&gt;Forbes has valued&lt;/a&gt; the former Beatle’s net worth at $1.4bn (£1.04bn), making him the world’s third richest musician behind Jay-Z at $2.8bn (£2.01bn) and Taylor Swift at $2bn (£1.49bn).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The magazine attributed McCartney’s wealth to his musical catalog, legal maneuvers, tours and art collection. The 84-year-old derives the bulk of his fortune from MPL Communications, the publishing company he founded in 1969 that manages his own catalog and those of other artists.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/nov/09/paul-mccartney-billionaire"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
